# Normalize line endings.  Git stores text with LF and checks it out with LF on every
# platform, so an editor that writes CRLF cannot leak carriage returns into a commit.
# Without this, a single edit to a CRLF file rewrites every line it touches and buries
# the real change in a whitespace-only diff.  Windows contributors are unaffected:
# modern editors and the Rust/Python toolchains all handle LF natively.
* text=auto

# Python type stubs for the compiled `_lib` extension are generated by
# `pyo3-stub-gen` (`make pystubs`) and committed so they ship in the wheel and can
# be reviewed. They must never be hand-edited: `make pystubs-check` regenerates them
# in CI and fails on any diff. Mark them generated so GitHub collapses them in diffs
# and excludes them from language statistics.
python/qiskit_fermions/_lib/**/*.pyi linguist-generated=true
